WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:15.190
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta,
horror stories cooked to perfection with a

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.740
splash of red sauce.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.570
My name is CZ, and I will be your server this
episode.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:27.460
This episode is brought to you by UltimateHallowenGuide.com
-- Your guide to all things Halloween.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.860
Valentine's Day.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.370
I've always thought we should just get rid
of it and add another Halloween in it’s

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.370
stead.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.970
However, we're stuck with it, it's February
and you clicked on this video, so here are

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.360
some Valentine's horror stories for you to
sink your teeth into.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:48.719
Let's dig right in.

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:51.300
Number One -- BLIND DATE

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.600
I'd always found the concept of a blind date
to be somewhat of a gamble.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.300
At best, it could lead to a very fun time,
and who knows, maybe even something more.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.460
But you run the risk of a terrible and awkward
hour or more, and you never know what you

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.520
might get.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.980
Tara and I exchanged names and phone numbers
online, then decided only to text each other

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.930
before the date in order to preserve the blind
aspect of the encounter.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:20.120
I arrived at the restaurant a few minutes
early to find that she was already there.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.570
We quickly got a table and sat down.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:26.660
After our initial introductions, one of the
first things she did was suggest that we both

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.050
turn off our phones for the remainder of the
date.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:33.830
While I was surprised at her progressive request,
I quickly agreed and powered down my device.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.460
I had been on all too many bad dates where
the girl had fallen back on looking at her

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.390
phone at the first hint of an awkward moment.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:44.030
I mean, I've been guilty of it too, so I figured
we may as well at least attempt to get to

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.900
know each other now that we had taken the
time to arrange a date.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.510
We started with the small talk.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:51.480
The city, our jobs, the obligatory stuff.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.960
Then she started to ask some weird questions.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.450
Questions like: Have you ever thought about
murdering someone?

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.260
I told her, we all have at some point… right?

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.950
In a joking manner of course.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.600
She went on about how planning the perfect
murder in her head was kind of a fun hobby

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.810
of hers.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.480
When she asked me how I would do it, I explained
that I kind of like the Alfred Hitchcock idea

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.569
of stabbing someone with an icicle.

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:18.930
I wasn't really sure what to think when I
heard what she said next.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.810
She told me, if you do it right, you've got
no reason to make the evidence disappear."

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:28.200
Of course, I was curious as to where she was
going with this.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.520
"These detectives always look for a motive,”
she explained.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.661
“So you simply have to have no reason to
be there, no connection to the person, and

00:02:37.661 --> 00:02:43.240
of course, no witnesses."

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:49.490
While it would be easy to get away with something
like that, I did have to wonder why would

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.630
you want to kill a random person?"

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.390
She just said that she finds it kind of exciting.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:57.370
It's not that I didn't realize this conversation
was weird…

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:01.010
Normally, I wouldn't find myself talking about
such things with a girl...

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.850
Nonetheless on the first date.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:06.569
But, for whatever reason, I didn't really
mind discussing it with her.

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:09.060
I even found it kind of fun.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.990
At the end of the date I picked up the bill.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.870
And she asked if I had any plans for the rest
of the night.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:18.300
Taking the hint, I invited her back to my
place, and before long, we were off.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:23.630
Upon arriving home I stepped into the bathroom
to freshen up and brush my teeth, just in

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:24.630
case.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.730
While I was in there, I turned my phone back
on to see if I had missed any messages while

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:28.760
I was out on the date.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:32.810
Tara was waiting for me out in the living
room, so I tried to be quick.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.599
I noticed just one message on my phone.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:37.760
It was from Tara.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.870
Thirty minutes ago.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.340
That's odd.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:43.349
We hadn't even left the restaurant thirty
minutes ago.

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:45.370
Both of our phones were off at the time.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.080
I opened the message.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.080
“Hey.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.580
I'm SO sorry I didn't make it.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.819
Someone slashed my tires.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:56.190
I tried calling but your phone was dead.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:00.240
Did you still want to try to meet up?”

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.160
As I tried to comprehend what I had just read,
I heard her doing something out in the kitchen.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.540
The sound of a drawer opening or something.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.959
I was about to go out there and find out what
she was doing rummaging through my stuff,

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:15.850
when a wave of realization hit me with a petrifying
force.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:21.100
“No reason to be there, no connection to
the person, no witnesses.”

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:25.620
I locked the bathroom door, grabbed my phone
and called up the number I had for Tara.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.620
It rang.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.189
Once, twice, three times.

00:04:28.189 --> 00:04:33.210
I started sweating bullets as I saw her shadow
appear from the crack under the door.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.949
She had made an effort to make sure all of
her movements were silent, then she just stood

00:04:36.949 --> 00:04:38.259
outside the door.

00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:43.560
After what seemed like ages, I heard a voice
on the other side of the line.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.560
“Hello?

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:45.560
Hello?”

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.770
The woman that picked up the phone was not
the same woman standing outside my bathroom

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.110
door.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.680
Not knowing what else to do I hung up the
phone and began to dial 9-1-1.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.860
She must have heard me dialing, because she
then grabbed the door handle and tried to

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.249
come into the bathroom.

00:04:59.249 --> 00:05:02.279
As soon as she realized it was locked, she
quickly moved away from the door.

00:05:02.279 --> 00:05:05.020
I braced myself for her to barge down the
door or something…

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:08.349
That’s when I heard my front door open and
quickly close.

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:12.150
I assumed that she had left, but I didn't
dare leave the safety of the locked bathroom

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.089
until the cops had arrived and locked down
the area.

00:05:15.089 --> 00:05:17.250
Of course, they found no trace of the woman.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.050
After telling the police my account of what
went on that night, I tried to get them to

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:24.400
take down a description of her appearance,
but I was told that there was no case.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.969
Since I had invited her in, she hadn't actually
broken any law.

00:05:27.969 --> 00:05:31.270
As far as I could tell nothing had been stolen.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.439
Besides, without knowing her name, or who
she actually was, it was unlikely they would

00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:37.009
have found her anyway.

00:05:37.009 --> 00:05:42.250
Eventually, I got in contact with the real
Tara, and told her about what happened.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:46.189
She was understanding when I said that I no
longer felt comfortable meeting up for a blind

00:05:46.189 --> 00:05:47.189
date.

00:05:47.189 --> 00:05:52.300
It's been a couple of days now since the incident
and I've had an uneasy feeling since then.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.349
I've barely gotten any sleep.

00:05:54.349 --> 00:05:57.919
Sometimes I think I hear the sound of my door
handle wiggling like someone is trying to

00:05:57.919 --> 00:06:03.199
get in, but when I get up to check on it,
the sound dissipates.

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:04.400
She knew where I lived now.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.490
What was to stop her from coming back and
finishing the job?

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:11.710
I tried to tell myself that the whole thing
was a cruel prank… that she was trying to

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:15.309
mess with me for her own entertainment, and
that she probably just wanted to scare me

00:06:15.309 --> 00:06:16.650
or something…

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.710
Until today.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:22.960
See, since that day, I haven’t really had
much of an appetite.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.900
I finally had the stomach to eat something
again and decided to go to the kitchen and

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.389
prepare something for myself…

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:39.979
when I found the kitchen knife put away in
the wrong drawer…

00:06:39.979 --> 00:06:43.539
Number 2 -- Heartbreaker

00:06:43.539 --> 00:06:48.330
The stereotypical version of Valentine’s
Day has always gotten on my nerves.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:54.439
For one, the ads never show gay couples and
I tend to get asked out by guys who don’t

00:06:54.439 --> 00:06:57.490
believe I’m actually gay.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:59.979
This year wasn’t different by much.

00:06:59.979 --> 00:07:05.669
I had to sit through class, which I spent
texting my girlfriend, Amy, going over our

00:07:05.669 --> 00:07:07.080
plans for the night.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:12.119
Our LGBTQ friends were having a dinner party
and we agreed to go.

00:07:12.119 --> 00:07:16.219
As I was getting up to leave after class,
one of the guys walked over to me.

00:07:16.219 --> 00:07:18.210
I don't know who he is.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:21.009
He's one of the quiet guys who sits in the
back.

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:24.779
He handed me a heart-shaped note reading “will
you be mine?”

00:07:24.779 --> 00:07:28.699
I sighed, noticing his friend nervously watching
in the back.

00:07:28.699 --> 00:07:31.059
Obviously, his friend was asking.

00:07:31.059 --> 00:07:33.879
“Sorry, but I have a girlfriend.”

00:07:33.879 --> 00:07:36.229
I tried to be nice about it.

00:07:36.229 --> 00:07:40.740
He went back to his friend and I could feel
a cold glare following me.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.620
I'm used to guys being rude, so I shrugged
it off.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.720
I went home and got ready for the night.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:51.819
It felt like something was staring at me from
outside and in the shadows.

00:07:51.819 --> 00:07:55.229
The feeling came back on and off throughout
the night.

00:07:55.229 --> 00:07:59.460
The party was amazing, lots of laughs and
booze.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:03.069
Everyone was intoxicated, especially Amy.

00:08:03.069 --> 00:08:05.689
As I drove her home, there was a car following
us.

00:08:05.689 --> 00:08:08.740
I could feel my hair standing on end.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:13.300
Every time we passed an intersection, I would
look back to see if it would turn.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.990
It finally turned when we were two blocks
from Amy's.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:23.449
I helped her inside and she complained constantly
that it was hot in her apartment, so I opened

00:08:23.449 --> 00:08:25.219
the window a bit.

00:08:25.219 --> 00:08:29.860
Most people would have made out and proceeded
to make love to their partner at this point,

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.020
but I have more dignity than that.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:34.460
I gave her a kiss goodnight and left.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:38.140
It was strangely quiet on my way home.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:43.079
The feeling of being followed was finally
gone, replaced by an uneasy feeling in my

00:08:43.079 --> 00:08:44.839
gut.

00:08:44.839 --> 00:08:47.410
Maybe the alcohol was finally kicking in.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:50.750
I got back to my dorm and cracked the window
open.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:55.240
The night air felt good on my warm face and
soothed my upset stomach.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.550
I decided to take a shot of whiskey before
going to bed.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:01.740
As I laid there, I thought I could hear the
door rattle.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:06.630
It was probably my imagination, the shot I
took couldn't have hit me that hard.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:10.089
Then again, that's also probably the alcohol.

00:09:10.089 --> 00:09:16.080
I wasn’t sure, but I thought I could see
the shadow of feet from underneath the door.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:21.810
I could have sworn something hit the window,
but it was probably just the wind.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:26.829
The morning light hit my eyes and the onset
of a hangover made my head throb.

00:09:26.829 --> 00:09:29.640
The slight smell of blood made me groan.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:32.660
It shouldn't be that time, yet.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:34.470
I got up just to make sure.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:42.319
Instead of the expected, the rug felt wet
under my feet and I discovered a heart on

00:09:42.319 --> 00:09:43.589
the floor.

00:09:43.589 --> 00:09:47.339
There was a knife through it and blood staining
my rug.

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:51.470
My heart was pounding as the metallic smell
flooded my senses.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:54.700
The breath caught in my throat and my stomach
twisted.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.842
I got up and rushed to the bathroom.

00:09:57.842 --> 00:10:00.070
The shock of it all made me sick, literally.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:05.600
I took a moment to drink some water after
painfully emptying the contents of my stomach,

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.860
hoping to ease the sense of dread knotting
it.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.709
I went back, pausing outside my door.

00:10:11.709 --> 00:10:16.990
It had been a long time since I last prayed
and right now, I was praying that it was nothing.

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:19.250
Praying that it was a delusion.

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:22.020
I opened the door and it was still there.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:26.470
I couldn’t stop myself from gagging and
that's when I saw the writing.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:33.029
The wall had blood smeared on it, reading:
“Now you can be mine...”

00:10:33.029 --> 00:10:37.900
The police came and they couldn't find any
evidence of forced entry.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.819
No trace of who did it was left behind.

00:10:40.819 --> 00:10:45.699
I found out that the heart belonged to Amy
and it was determined that they entered through

00:10:45.699 --> 00:10:46.750
the window.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:53.110
I'm not sure how anyone could climb 3 stories
from the outside of the building, but now

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:56.129
I never leave the window open at night.

00:10:56.129 --> 00:11:01.589
It’s been two years now and I even moved
to a different city because of rumors that

00:11:01.589 --> 00:11:02.839
I killed Amy.

00:11:02.839 --> 00:11:09.230
A new start was supposed to be a good thing,
until I found a heart-shaped note under my

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:16.920
door reading: “you are mine...”

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.449
Number 3 -- Dear Delilah

00:11:19.449 --> 00:11:22.610
Feb 8
Dear Delilah,

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:27.360
These February winds are cold, but I think
you will find the winds of change to be much

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:28.550
more comforting.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:33.029
Over the next week, pay close attention to
my instructions.

00:11:33.029 --> 00:11:38.399
If you do not falter I will reveal myself,
and we can spend the final night together,

00:11:38.399 --> 00:11:39.899
under the stars.

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:44.450
Tomorrow, I want you to look for my letter
where he sends up smoke signals, but they

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:49.730
aren't signals for help, in fact, he doesn’t
want them to be seen at all.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:51.269
Sincerely,
Hawkeye

00:11:51.269 --> 00:11:55.889
Feb 9
Dear Delilah,

00:11:55.889 --> 00:12:02.430
I know you will find this letter before he
does, for you see old habits do die hard.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:08.769
Every evening between the hours of 10 and
11PM, he steps outside to send up smoke signals.

00:12:08.769 --> 00:12:14.009
Every morning between 10 and 11, you step
outside to sweep his cigarette butts off of

00:12:14.009 --> 00:12:15.009
the porch.

00:12:15.009 --> 00:12:16.339
You've done well to look here.

00:12:16.339 --> 00:12:23.340
I know this because old habits do die hard
you see and I too have a habit, a habit of

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.339
watching you.

00:12:25.339 --> 00:12:29.720
He may need to fill himself with poison in
order to go on, but I know you have no need

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.880
for poison in your life.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:36.850
Your next letter will be waiting for you in
the post office, but only if you demonstrate

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:41.550
that you are willing to kick old habits by
skipping the day of the hour of habits.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.050
I'll be watching.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:45.720
Sincerely,
Hawkeye

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:49.050
Feb 11
Dear Delilah,

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:53.970
If you are reading this, you have impressed
me with your discipline.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:59.209
The day of the hour of habits has passed,
and he has not even taken the time to recognise

00:12:59.209 --> 00:13:01.319
its significance.

00:13:01.319 --> 00:13:05.410
Perhaps it's time for you to test his discipline.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:08.910
Inside this envelope, you will find a thin
but powerful magnet.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:13.310
If you want to test his discipline, glue this
magnet to the edge of your door before your

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:16.819
consciousness falls victim to the late hours.

00:13:16.819 --> 00:13:21.569
If he lacks discipline amid your innocent
slumber the magnet should slam the door shut

00:13:21.569 --> 00:13:24.069
behind him during his moonlit betrayal.

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:29.340
For your own safety, do not follow, but instead,
take note of the time.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:32.800
This will correspond to the address of my
next letter.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:36.730
You need not leave this street, but only drive
West in order to find it.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:41.029
As always, I will be watching...

00:13:41.029 --> 00:13:43.210
Sincerely,
Hawkeye

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.579
Feb 12
Dear Delilah,

00:13:47.579 --> 00:13:49.949
You've done well to make it this far.

00:13:49.949 --> 00:13:54.579
I understand the difficulty he has put you
through, but you have nearly reached the final

00:13:54.579 --> 00:13:57.839
night, upon which I will reveal myself to
you...

00:13:57.839 --> 00:13:59.699
Under the stars.

00:13:59.699 --> 00:14:04.850
To this point I have had you on the lookout
for my incoming letters, but now I do ask

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:09.009
you to do that which he has not and examine
the letters going out.

00:14:09.009 --> 00:14:14.009
You may be surprised to find him engaging
with a less advanced form of communication,

00:14:14.009 --> 00:14:20.000
however maybe when I ask you to track a physical
envelope to its destination, you'll understand

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:25.620
why a simple text message or email wouldn't
mask his efforts quite like a good old fashioned

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:27.589
piece of mail.

00:14:27.589 --> 00:14:32.139
Inside this envelope, you'll find a microscopic
GPS tracking device.

00:14:32.139 --> 00:14:34.860
The rest is up to you.

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:37.079
I'll be watching...

00:14:37.079 --> 00:14:38.560
Sincerely,
Hawkeye

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:41.519
Feb 13
Dear Delilah,

00:14:41.519 --> 00:14:48.850
I must say, I am quite impressed with your
resourcefulness.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:52.689
Even I may have never thought of sticking
the tracker on the bottom side of the last

00:14:52.689 --> 00:14:54.449
postage stamp in the house.

00:14:54.449 --> 00:15:00.720
You've worked hard to find this destination,
and your cleverness will not go in vain.

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.740
Old habits do die hard, you see.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.890
He is here, right now as you read this.

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:10.910
But you need not worry, as he is passed out.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.540
As is she.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.069
I've made sure of it.

00:15:14.069 --> 00:15:15.720
I've been watching.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:22.060
But before I can reveal myself to you, I have
but one final request.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:25.389
Consider the form factor of a cigarette.

00:15:25.389 --> 00:15:29.589
The inside is filled with disgusting, disposable
poison.

00:15:29.589 --> 00:15:35.430
It's wrapped tightly in a thin sheet of paper,
then ignited and burned all the way through.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:39.579
In fact, a small cigarette is not much different
than a large cigarette.

00:15:39.579 --> 00:15:44.130
Both are filled with disgusting, disposable
poison.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.879
Anything can be used to wrap a large cigarette.

00:15:46.879 --> 00:15:47.939
Bedsheets.

00:15:47.939 --> 00:15:48.990
Blankets.

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:50.040
Pillowcases.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.310
To be quite honest, it doesn't really matter.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:58.170
But what does matter, is that both large and
small cigarettes are burned.

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:00.509
All the way through.

00:16:00.509 --> 00:16:04.569
I'm sure you've already found the contents
of this envelope.

00:16:04.569 --> 00:16:06.970
This will be my final letter.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:11.879
Place all of my letters inside the large cigarette
before burning it through.

00:16:11.879 --> 00:16:15.180
I think you will find the winds of change
to be comforting.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:20.620
Tomorrow night, I will meet you at the grave
site and reveal myself to you.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:23.490
Then we can spend the night together.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:25.379
Under the stars.

00:16:25.379 --> 00:16:26.910
Sincerely,
Hawkeye

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:38.370
Thanks for listening to Al Dente Creepypasta.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:44.509
Your total comes out to $2.14, but if you
like this video right now, I’ll waive that

00:16:44.509 --> 00:16:47.129
fee and give you everything you just listened
to absolutely free.

00:16:47.129 --> 00:16:55.759
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every other week, ring that death-bell

00:16:55.759 --> 00:16:57.050
for notifications; I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:59.399
Assuming, we both survive.

